Let's build a Basic Vehicle Management System. This is the cleanest example to learn the Strategy Pattern (Inheritance) because everyone understands the difference between a Car and a Truck.
We will use InheritanceType.SINGLE_TABLE first. This is the most common strategy.
🎯 The Goal
We want to save Car and Truck objects.
 * Car: Has seatingCapacity.
 * Truck: Has payloadCapacity.
 * Database: We want ONE table (vehicle) that holds both, using a "Discriminator Column" to tell them apart.
📂 1. The Entities (The Strategy Pattern Implementation)
A. The Parent (Vehicle)
This is where the Strategy is defined.
package org.adesh.vehicle.Model;

import jakarta.persistence.*;
import lombok.Getter;
import lombok.Setter;

@Entity
@Getter
@Setter
// 1. THE STRATEGY: We choose Single Table (One big bucket)
@Inheritance(strategy = InheritanceType.SINGLE_TABLE) 
// 2. THE TAG: We create a special column 'vehicle_type' to identify rows
@DiscriminatorColumn(name = "vehicle_type", discriminatorType = DiscriminatorType.STRING)
public abstract class Vehicle {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    private String manufacturer;
    private String model;
}

B. The Child (Car)
package org.adesh.vehicle.Model;

import jakarta.persistence.DiscriminatorValue;
import jakarta.persistence.Entity;
import lombok.Getter;
import lombok.Setter;

@Entity
@Getter
@Setter
// 3. THE VALUE: If we save this class, put "CAR" in the 'vehicle_type' column
@DiscriminatorValue("CAR") 
public class Car extends Vehicle {
    
    private int seatingCapacity;
}

C. The Child (Truck)
package org.adesh.vehicle.Model;

import jakarta.persistence.DiscriminatorValue;
import jakarta.persistence.Entity;
import lombok.Getter;
import lombok.Setter;

@Entity
@Getter
@Setter
// 3. THE VALUE: If we save this class, put "TRUCK" in the 'vehicle_type' column
@DiscriminatorValue("TRUCK") 
public class Truck extends Vehicle {
    
    private double payloadCapacity;
}

📂 2. The Repository
Notice we only need ONE repository for the Parent!
